 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? That's usually turpentine residue from thinning the paint. It' not a coating, so it doesn't ling like a varnish. You can fix it. Clean the surface with rubbing alcohol and then repaint the area. Yes, touch up paint in a small pot. Dab a cotton bud with a little paint and see how it looks. Use a really thin layer of thin paint and sand it lightly after it's dry. Gloss dries much clearer.",
